{#
  Popover macro — a floating content box anchored to a trigger element.

  HTML tag: <div role="dialog">
  CSS class: popover
  Popover API: this macro renders popover="auto", so the browser manages
    open/close state with no script: top layer while open, Escape and a
    click outside close it (light dismiss). A trigger button names it with
    command="toggle-popover" commandfor="{id}" (Chrome 135, Firefox 144,
    Safari 26.2) and popovertarget="{id}" (Chrome 114, Firefox 125,
    Safari 17), which engines without command/commandfor use instead.
  Accessibility:
    - role="dialog"; params.label or labelledBy names it.
    - The browser exposes the trigger's expanded state from popovertarget,
      so the trigger needs no static aria-expanded (it would go stale).

  Params:
    id             string   Element id. Required so a trigger can
                            target it via popovertarget="...".
    popover        string   "auto" (default) | "manual" | "hint".
    label          string   Accessible name (aria-label).
    labelledBy     string   aria-labelledby target.
    classes        string
    attributes     object

  Body content: heading, body, and close control via caller().

  Usage:
    {% from "components/popover/macro.njk" import popover %}
    <button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="info"
            command="toggle-popover" commandfor="info" popovertarget="info">Details</button>
    {% call popover({ id: "info", label: "Details" }) %}
      <p>More information about this item.</p>
    {% endcall %}
#}
{%- macro popover(params) -%}
<div
  class="popover{% if params.classes %} {{ params.classes }}{% endif %}"
  id="{{ params.id }}"
  role="dialog"
  popover="{{ params.popover | default('auto') }}"
  {%- if params.labelledBy %} aria-labelledby="{{ params.labelledBy }}"
  {%- elif params.label %} aria-label="{{ params.label }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if params.attributes %}{% for k, v in params.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
  {%- if params.html -%}{{ params.html | safe }}
  {%- elif caller -%}{{ caller() }}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
